<title>FINLAND: NOKIA PLANS MEXICAN ASSEMBLY WORKSHOP.</title>
<headline>NOKIA PLANS MEXICAN ASSEMBLY WORKSHOP.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecommunications group Nokia Oy plans to build a small assembly plant mainly for batteries and mobile phone accessories in Reynosa, Mexico where labour costs are low, a Nokia spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Calling it a plant would be the overstatement of the day, it is more like a workshop,&quot; the spokesman said. He was commenting on a report about Nokia's plans in daily Kauppalehti.</p>
<p>The investment is minor and the operation will be marginally small, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 242</p>
</text>
